<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <fullName>Question_Type__c</fullName>
    <description>What kind of question the answer belongs to, so reports can sort and filter by it. Set from the source field&apos;s name for the fields the package ships: a scale series takes its family (Satisfaction, Confidence, Rating and the rest); the other series take the kind of response, each spanning more than one data type (Yes / No for the yes or no picklists and the checkboxes, Numeric Response for numbers and percents, Date Response for dates, Custom Response for text, long text and links); a single field takes its subject (Demographics, Contact, Address and the rest). Left blank for a field the package does not ship. Not restricted, so a customer&apos;s own before-save flow on Form Submission Answer can write a type of its own for its own fields.</description>
    <inlineHelpText>The kind of question: a scale family such as Satisfaction or Confidence, or a subject such as Demographics. Blank for your own fields unless your automation fills it.</inlineHelpText>
    <label>Question Type</label>
